  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Little change to the forecast reasoning and\nsynoptic setups through Thu. Where guidance is fairly well \nclustered is with an amplified upper trough that will be \nshifting east out of the Central U.S. A progressive and open \nwave will sweep through the Eastern U.S at the end of the week. \nBefore that happens, low level flow is currently veering\nsoutheast to south today as weak warm front/coastal trough \nlifts through, which is producing some widely sct showers.\nAny showers dissipate by evening, then a fog and low stratus\nthreat later this evening to Thu morning as moistening boundary\nlayer continues. Area is firmly entrenched in srly flow Thu, \nbut with no forcing in place, pops are generally less than 20%,\nthough can't rule out a quick light shower anywhere. Very warm\nthrough Thursday with highs around 80 interior to 70s beaches.\nOvernight lows will be especially above climo, with readings in\nthe 60s the next few nights, and where we should be for\nafternoon highs.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Friday - Still looks like widespread showers \nand a few thunderstorms breaking out during the afternoon into \nevening with a wet cold front moving through. Anomalous \nmoisture and higher- than- normal instability for early \nNovember is expected, as indicated by EFI highlighting CAPE \nvals nearing the 80th percentile. Have increased the thunder \nthreat for inland areas where the EFI is highlighting the higher\nCAPE/Shear indices inland, and where highest instability and\nshear will reside. If best forcing lines up with peak heating, \na strong to severe thunderstorm threat would materialize for \nareas esp west of Hwy 17 Fri afternoon. Main threat would be \ndamaging winds. \n\nFront sweeps offshore late Fri evening with any remaining\nshowers exiting the OBX before daybreak Sat.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Good agreement amongst models with fropa late\nFri, which will usher in a more seasonably dry airmass for the \ncoming weekend. Return to mo sunny skies and highs in the upper\n60s to low 70s Sat, then cooler yet for Sun with 60-65. Lows\nwill be in the 40s, with some 30s for some of the normally\ncolder spots.",
